WEBVTT

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.300
Sorry to interrupt
while you're waxing sentimental, devil boy.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:19.840
DEVIL BOY

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.090
What in the world happened?

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.350
You probably can't help
brooding over that snail girl, but...

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.770
I'd prefer that you didn't commit double-suicide
with some local girl because of it.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.230
That's such a glaring misunderstanding.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.100
DON'T SAY SOME LOCAL GIRL.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.980
KANBARU IS A CUTE UNDERCLASSMAN.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.820
This is Suruga Kanbaru.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.570
Oh, I see. So this is Gaen's niece.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.570
Previously Suruga Gaen,

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.790
and once Gaen's big sister
finished the marriage paperwork, Suruga Kanbaru.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.660
So Ononoki, what are you doing here?

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.130
Oh, it's just a coincidence.
I wasn't planning on rescuing you, devil boy.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.960
I was just doing my job.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:04.470
At the job site, devil boy was trying to commit
double suicide with a girl I didn't know.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.260
And I thought,
"Yahoo, I just have to get in the way."

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.560
In any case, thank you, Ononoki.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.060
I keep owing you favors,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.600
but someday, I'll make sure
to repay you for this favor.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.980
If you say you're going to repay me,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.240
normally I'd like for you
to pile up a giant fortune.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.110
But this time, I'll let you off the hook
if you answer my question.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.410
What in the world happened?

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.260
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.010
SHINOBU MAIL, PART TWO

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.140
An armor-clad samurai?

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.140
An armor-clad samurai that automatically
rebuilds itself when broken up

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.060
and has the energy drain skill?

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.150
Yeah.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.360
<i>However, I didn't tell Ononoki everything.</i>

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.700
<i>I hesitated about relating
to Ononoki the situation</i>

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.080
<i>that I hadn't prepared my heart for.</i>

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.500
<i>The armor-clad samurai's parting words.</i>

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.170
<i>An impossible array
of the alphabet... "Kiss-shot."</i>

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.080
KISS-SHOT

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.340
<i>That name not even I call her by anymore...
is what was said.</i>

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.840
<i>And then, the demon sword "Kokoro Watari"...</i>

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.010
Ononoki, do you have any ideas?

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.550
That armor-clad samurai...

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.600
Does it have something to do
with the job you're currently entrusted with?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.850
It does.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:22.980
Yup, that's right...
Indeed, it does. It's within my duties.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.400
But listening to that story,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.820
it's almost completely different
from the phenomenon

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.610
that was the subject of my field work.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:36.410
It seems it's become much more violent
since I was investigating it.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.910
What happened in these past few days?

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.920
In the first place, it wasn't even
an armor-clad samurai when I was chasing it.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.260
You know, Ononoki.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.920
What is it, devil boy?

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.260
Can I drop this particular case?

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:58.270
Oh no, don't get me wrong. I'm fine.
I'm perfectly fine, but... Kanbaru...

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.810
We can let Kanbaru go home now, right?

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.110
What's that?

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.190
In other words, devil boy,

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.820
you're going to scrap the promise
you made with Gaen?

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:12.860
Going to scrap...

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.080
Saying that you would
introduce that girl to her,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.080
you borrowed some wisdom
from Gaen, right?

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:23.040
It was absolutely necessary
in order to save Mayoi Hachikuji.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.880
So you didn't actually have a choice,
but still, a promise is a promise.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.510
You've really got some nerve, devil boy.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.010
For you to break a promise you made to Gaen
almost makes me fall for you.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.270
I don't plan on breaking that promise.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.730
You have good pectorals.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.190
Don't touch on the subject of my pecs.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.480
I want to touch it.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.360
Don't show an abnormal amount
of interest in muscles.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.780
I'm a corpse, so showing an interest in meat
is like an instinct...

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:55.410
So what's the reason?

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.700
The reason you want to break the promise
you made with Gaen.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:04.460
I'm more than happy to introduce
Kanbaru to her, even now.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.380
But the promise wasn't just that, right?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.670
She was trying to make Kanbaru help
with the job going on over on your end.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.180
<i>Gaen had said</i>

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.930
<i>that she needed Kanbaru's "left hand,"
that is, her "left arm."</i>

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:22.560
<i>Of course, I was the one that made use
of Gaen's wisdom and knowledge.</i>

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.480
<i>Kanbaru had nothing to do with it.</i>

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.360
<i>Therefore, the promise was made with the condition
that Kanbaru herself agree to do so.</i>

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.190
<i>But that was a mistake to begin with.</i>

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:36.280
<i>I knew extremely well
that Kanbaru would never refuse</i>

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.410
<i>if I requested something from her.</i>

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:43.330
<i>As a result, I subjected Kanbaru
to unthinkable danger.</i>

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.460
<i>I completely roped her in.</i>

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.880
<i>As her upperclassman,
I was supposed to decline such an offer.</i>

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.260
I understand how you feel, devil boy.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.340
But you should give up on that.
I can't recommend it.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.510
This is a warning to you as a friend.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.970
I don't remember ever
becoming friends with you.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:06.020
Devil boy, I've thought of you
as a friend for a while now, you know?

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.020
It's way past the point of no return.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:15.360
Why hasn't it crossed your mind that
even if you were to send that girl home,

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.030
that may not be protecting her?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.740
What do you mean?

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.040
An apparition affects only by looking,
curses only by meeting.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.870
And yet, that girl touched
that armor-clad samurai, didn't she?

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.090
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.250
<i>So Suruga Kanbaru already has...</i>

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.250
...NOT ONLY DID SHE TOUCH, SHE PUNCHED.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.010
<i>...gotten herself involved.</i>

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.010
PUNCHED

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.380
Devil boy, sit up straight.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.590
Sit up straight. Hurry.

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:41.470
Hurry up.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:43.350
Hurry, hurry.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:43.850
HURRY, HURRY

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:50.310
Hold on just a second. It will be real quick.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.740
Um, Ononoki...

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:01.660
Don't think you can go back in time or anything.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.870
Just like the case with Mayoi Hachikuji...
Devil boy, you don't have enough resolve.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.630
Hey, you, you're thinking you can
restart your life at any time, aren't you?

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:16.380
You're thinking no matter when you start,
you'll never be late, aren't you?

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:22.100
Even if you make a mistake, even if you're careless,
maybe you think you can make something of it?

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.680
In the end, the positives
and negatives of life even out, you say?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:32.520
Of course, it's a given
that it turns to zero when you die.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:44.160
So devil boy,
if you really care about that girl,

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.200
don't be irresponsible
and send her home right now.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.040
There's more reason to take her
to where Gaen is now.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.880
And have Gaen protect her.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.340
Have Gaen...

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:58.550
Right. Don't scrap the promise,
and have the girl be protected.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.180
PROTECT (HOGO)

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:01.800
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.140
<i>If we're talking about irresponsible,</i>

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.680
<i>sending Kanbaru home now
would be much more irresponsible.</i>

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.350
I DIDN'T SEEK THE FREEDOM TO RUIN MY ENTIRE LIFE
BY BREAKING A PROMISE I MADE TO GAEN.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.020
BUT THAT ASIDE,
I WANT TO KEEP MY PROMISE.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.680
I SHOULD KEEP IT.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.230
<i>No... I'll be honest here.</i>

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.520
<i>It was a given I didn't want Kanbaru involved
in something with a dangerous armor-clad samurai.</i>

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:19.280
<i>Then, asking whether or not
I wanted to be involved myself,</i>

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.240
<i>it's definitely the case that I don't.</i>

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.070
<i>If anything, it's that I can't help
but be involved in this.</i>

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.080
HE ENTRUSTED ME WITH A MESSAGE.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.080
A MESSAGE TO "MY MASTER."

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:30.830
<i>If the true nature of that armor-clad samurai
really is what I think it is...</i>

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.920
<i>Even if I think such a thing is impossible,</i>

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.670
<i>if even the slightest possibility
that it can be exists...</i>

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.420
<i>I can't discard that.</i>

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.760
<i>Until I know that... I can't go home.</i>

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.430
Looks like you've reached a conclusion.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.480
Oh boy, friends really are troublesome.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:56.480
Starting now, I'll chase the armor-clad samurai
apparition you supposedly witnessed, devil boy.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:09:00.400
Based on how it disappeared,
I don't think I can find it,

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.150
but it's my job to go on a fool's errand.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.160
It's my job to step on devil boy's face
and to go on a fool's errand.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:08.240
Stop saying that!

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:09.910
And don't step on my face
as part of your job!

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:16.170
So devil boy, you should carry that niece
and meet up with Gaen.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.920
And explain to her what the situation is.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:22.670
When you say it that way,
it sounds like Kanbaru is my niece...

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:30.270
In any case, both you guys and I
should leave this place pretty soon.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.270
IT'S FINE TO WAX SENTIMENTAL FOREVER
IN FRONT OF THE BURNED RUINS.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:35.190
Soon, things like firefighters
and the police will be rushing over.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.070
Understanding when to retreat
is a must for a specialist.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.040
Oh, you came to?

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.790
Oh, Araragi-senpai! Are you OK?

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.050
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.100
I don't understand the situation very well,

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.770
but my instincts are telling me
I shouldn't miss this opportunity.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.730
Your instincts are amazing...

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:15.390
WHAT ARE THEY TELLING HER?

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:15.980
THEY'RE SAYING TOO MUCH.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.900
I don't think I can quite walk yet.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.650
I'll just sit here
and get a piggyback ride for a while.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.860
Oh, fine... Just a little bit longer, okay?

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:30.660
The physical aspect aside,
it's a definite that I'm exhausted mentally.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.620
Somehow, I'm feeling out of whack.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.000
Out of whack?

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.960
In some way, I'm reminded
of the North Shirahebi Shrine.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.380
Araragi-senpai...

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:46.630
Am I proceeding toward that someone
you wanted to introduce to me?

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.390
Oh... Yeah, we are.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.640
But about that, Kanbaru,
I need to apologize to you.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.890
No need for apologies.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.350
In fact, I'd rather you didn't apologize.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:02.900
Making you bow your head, Araragi-senpai,
would be a disgrace for Suruga Kanbaru.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.240
If so, wouldn't me giving you
a piggyback ride

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.660
be more of a disgrace for Suruga Kanbaru?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:08.820
KANBARU / SURUGA

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.660
You'd be so disgraced
you're splintered or something?

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:15.540
No, in all seriousness, it may be more dangerous
to send you back right now.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:19.620
At the least, until we figure out the situation,
I want you to accompany me.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:24.170
For every favor you ask of me, Araragi-senpai,
this is how I answer:

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:25.630
Eat up!

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:26.800
Shut up!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.130
Also, that's cute!

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.180
WHAT IN THE WORLD DID I ORDER?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:35.930
But I'll at least ask you
where we're headed, Araragi-senpai.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.100
Right now, we're headed
to the aforementioned rendezvous point.

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:43.270
Let's see... You probably know of it.
It's called Rouhaku Park.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:44.520
Rouhaku?

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.400
It might be Namishiro.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.820
Apparently it was Senjyogahara's neighborhood
back in middle school.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.030
Then I might remember if I saw it.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:57.080
In any case, roger that, Araragi-senpai.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.540
Right now, we're headed to that park, right?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.880
And the person you wanted me
to meet will be there?

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.040
Well, yeah.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.550
But, if so, Araragi-senpai...

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.720
Aren't you going in
the completely opposite direction?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.930
Huh? But...

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:18.310
I guess we'll go back a bit
and correct the route... I'm sorry, Kanbaru.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.480
Well, it's no big deal.
I trust you with everything.

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.690
Araragi-senpai, do as you want.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.940
ONE HOUR LATER

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.450
<i>We ended up in a location
that we didn't know.</i>

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:40.910
Come to think, Araragi-senpai,
didn't you get lost in the past, or not?

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:44.130
Didn't you say you were about to, but didn't,
or something like that?

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.840
You know, with Hachikuji...

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:52.840
<i>No, wait. The lost cow isn't here any longer.</i>

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:53.720
<i>But...</i>

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:58.640
You shouldn't make any detours
and go straight home as well!

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.390
<i>No, but...</i>

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:05.650
<i>Would he actually set up something like this,
that's more malicious than harassing?</i>

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:11.490
<i>Besides, even if this "lost" bit is his doing,
I don't see the objective for doing so.</i>

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:17.240
<i>What is he planning to do with me and Kanbaru
after we lose our way... after we're lost?</i>

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.450
Kanbaru, I'm letting go.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.450
Of the daikon?

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.500
No, I mean you.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:23.500
IF ANYTHING, NOT A DAIKON BUT AN ANTELOPE.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.380
EARLIER, EARLIER TO GIVE UP THE BETTER

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.380
CALLING

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.010
IZUKO GAEN

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.510
<i>Hey, Koyomin...</i>

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.640
<i>I've been waiting for you.
I was anxiously waiting.</i>

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:41.140
<i>I thought it was about time you called me.</i>

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:47.770
<i>So? How is it going right now?
Do tell Big Sister Gaen.</i>

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:48.900
Let's see...

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:50.030
IZUKO GAEN
CRAB

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.530
IZUKO GAEN
SNAIL

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.650
IZUKO GAEN
MONKEY

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:53.650
IZUKO GAEN
SNAKE

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:54.400
IZUKO GAEN
CAT

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:58.070
What do you actually know?

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.660
<i>I know everything, as you may know.</i>

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:08.920
<i>That's a joke, a joke.
Why are you getting so serious, Koyomin?</i>

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:13.170
<i>If I say five things, one is sure to be correct.
It's a dirty tactic adults use.</i>

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:17.430
<i>Personally, I'd predict that it's the snail.</i>

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:17.930
SNAIL - LOST COW

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.930
<i>She got it right.</i>

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:23.560
<i>Simple. I thought the only one
you'd have the luxury</i>

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.100
<i>to make a phone call
seeking help would be the snail.</i>

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:29.400
<i>Just an analogy. So, how is it?</i>

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.690
That's exactly what it is... Yes.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:33.650
Right now, together with Kanbaru,

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:36.820
I was heading to the park
where we were supposed to meet up.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.820
But for over an hour now...

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:39.820
IZUKO GAEN

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:44.080
I was imagining what kind
of thing it would be, but...

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.790
of all those I imagined,
that's the smallest one.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.420
Koyomin.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:51.380
Hurry up and join me, please.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.800
I want to hear the details
face-to-face now.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:59.800
No, I mean, the story is such that
joining you is what I can't do right now.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.220
That was why I was seeking
some advice from you—

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.520
<i>This isn't worth me giving advice.</i>

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.060
<i>It's merely someone
meddling in your affairs.</i>

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:10.060
<i>If you can't overcome that small an obstacle
by yourself, I'd be troubled.</i>

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:14.190
<i>Fortunately, this isn't the first time
you're getting lost on your way.</i>

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.280
Koyomin,

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:19.820
<i>follow Meme's principle here
and help yourself on your own.</i>

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:20.820
No...

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.030
IZUKO GAEN

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.910
<i>You're not alone.</i>

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:27.330
<i>That's right, you have your reliable underclassman
beside you right now.</i>

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.790
<i>Then, you can rely on her.</i>

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.540
R-Rely on her, but...

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.920
What do you think Kanbaru is?
Kanbaru is—

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:40.050
IZUKO GAEN

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.050
<i>Such a pity to keep talent like that dormant.</i>

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.060
SHE JUST HUNG UP ON ME

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.480
Oh, so your phone call is over, Araragi-senpai?

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:53.610
And that look on your face...
I assume you need something from your slave.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.530
I don't have any slaves.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:59.360
Then you don't need my opinion?
That's so reassuring.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:00.860
No, I don't—

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:08.120
I do need it. Kanbaru,
if you have any thoughts, let me know.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.930
All right, I know. This way.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:27.020
I don't know the way to the park,

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:31.480
but if it's near where
Senjyogahara-senpai's old house was...

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.810
I know the approximate direction by scent.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:34.810
Let's go!

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:37.570
It's not by sight, but scent?

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:46.740
Come on, Araragi-senpai.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:47.830
ARE YOU A NINJA OR SOMETHING?

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:53.330
Araragi-senpai, the apparition called the lost cow
makes people lose their way, right?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.540
Then all you have to do
is to not go down the normal paths.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:04.680
<i>Around three in the morning, at last...</i>

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:05.430
NAMISHIRO (ROUHAKU) PARK

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.260
<i>...we arrived at the park.</i>

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:09.390
Huh?

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:17.110
Of all things, it's only been three hours
since I made the phone call.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.400
She couldn't possibly have gotten impatient
and left already.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.150
But Araragi-senpai,

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:25.240
most people would go home if they were forced
to wait for three hours in the middle of the night.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.990
If you say so, that may be true, but...

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.160
<i>I know.</i>

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.660
<i>Just like I got lost on my way,</i>

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:35.790
<i>maybe Gaen, who we were going to meet,
met some sort of apparition phenomenon.</i>

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:38.750
<i>Is it unthinkable that possibility
is what's causing her not to be here?</i>

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:41.010
Kanbaru, I have a favor to ask.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.470
Eat up!

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.010
That's not it.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:48.510
It may be useless, but I'd like to split up
and comb the entire park.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.220
If you find something, holler at me.

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:51.980
So I just need to scream?

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.730
Don't scream. I'd be the one that gets arrested.

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:56.860
Roger. Will serve you.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:57.360
ARRESTED (TSUKAMARU)

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:57.770
SERVE (TSUKAMATSURU)

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.240
Araragi-senpai! Found her!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.040
It doesn't look like there's anyone there...

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.250
No, no, Araragi-senpai.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:18.710
See? Look closely.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:22.960
Sh-Shinobu!

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.760
Oh, if it isn't my master! You're pretty late.

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:37.310
<i>She's so cute...</i>

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.070
Hey, Shinobu.
Why in the world are you here...

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.320
Ka ka!

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.740
Monkey, huh...

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.330
That gave me a hard time for sure.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:58.080
Indeed, I found this kitten
to be one tough customer.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.830
A cat, indeed...

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:05.880
LET'S PUT ASIDE THE PERVERT FOR NOW.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:10.050
Well, you know... by "monkey"
I'm not talking about this girl.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:13.850
It was wearing a raincoat and galoshes,
but it was someone other than her.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:14.770
Someone else?

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.310
In any case, it was an apparition
I'd been fighting

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:20.520
somewhere out there until just recently,
together with the cat.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:22.520
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:23.530
AND A CAT?

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:24.530
WHAT CAT?

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:25.530
WHAT IN THE WORLD IS GOING ON
IN THIS TOWN RIGHT NOW?

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:28.530
It was a competition you'd dream of,
in all sorts of ways.

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:32.410
Well, this is nothing more than a scratch,
nothing serious.

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:34.910
What about on your end? Were you all right?

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:40.790
Y-Yeah. After parting ways with you...
Let's see. About that darkness...

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:41.670
No need.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:44.250
I was briefed on that already.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:48.340
It seems I've had all sorts
of misunderstandings for over 400 years now.

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:50.260
The epitome of clumsiness, indeed.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.180
You heard? From whom—

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:54.680
I don't have to even tell you.

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:58.730
I heard from the little girl
who stomped on you.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.900
The little girl who stomped on me?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.440
Well, I have no idea what you're talking about...

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:07.190
Shinobu, you're the only one
that's stomped on me with a bare foot, you know?

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.650
I didn't say it was a bare foot.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:14.580
Drats! So this is what they mean by the saying
"the tongue ever turns to the aching tooth"!

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.830
Though it looks like
you're aching as much as you can ache...

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:22.750
More like, you have a cute footprint
clearly left on your face.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.000
What the...!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.250
Yeah...

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:32.510
I secretly wondered this whole time
what happened while I was unconscious.

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:35.430
If you saw it, then say something!

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:38.560
You just continued riding piggyback
on your upperclassman, thinking it was funny?

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.350
Well, normally a marking of that sort

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:45.650
would be so resentful that
I'd want to peel the skin off your face.

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:49.940
But against my will,
the doll-girl has saved us...

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:53.030
So this one time,
I'll graciously forgive her.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.120
"Has saved us"? Come now...

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:58.540
What really happened to you, Shinobu?

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.670
Well, it's not worth mentioning.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:07.420
While the cat and I were being
assaulted by a monkey...

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:09.420
When we were having a tough time...

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:15.140
That doll-girl suddenly appeared,
and, impressively enough, joined forces with us.

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:18.520
What was that special move of hers?

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:18.890
"A RULEBOOK MOSTLY FILLED WITH EXCEPTIONS"

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:21.810
"Unlimited Rulebook," or something?

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:24.230
She used it to blow off
the right half of the monkey's body.

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.610
And, after she saved you,

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:31.190
Ononoki told you what's happened
since that incident, or something?

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:32.490
Then...

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:35.780
<i>Assuming she heard about the darkness there,</i>

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:39.580
<i>then, did she hear about
the armor-clad samurai afterwards as well?</i>

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:43.120
<i>No, that doesn't seem to be the case.</i>

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:45.670
Well, I'm glad both of us
are safe and sound.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.800
No, I guess we're not quite safe just yet.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:52.510
Apparently, the so-called master
of the Hawaiian-shirt boy

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.510
is going to restore the pairing
between you and me?

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:59.510
Doll-girl said that it'd be good
to meet up with you for that reason.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:04.770
Yet, I arrive here,
and neither you or that master are around.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:05.770
So...

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:09.900
So... that's why you were sleeping
under the swings?

00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:11.360
What kind of idea is that?

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:13.280
How do you think
outside the box like that?

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:15.280
Even if you were tired
from an unexpected battle,

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.490
at the least, if you're going to sleep,
there are other places—

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:20.950
Master, we should talk about that later.

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:24.870
Unfortunately, it seems
we're not quite done fighting just yet...

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:28.630
It seems the battle isn't quite over just yet.

00:22:29.710 --> 00:24:20.187
The battle for us seems to be
what's coming up now.
